 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The regular past",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about finished events, use the past: **Jeg jobbet i går** («I worked yesterday»). Many verbs form the past with **-et** or **-te**: jobbe → jobbet, kjøpe → kjøpte.",
      "The verb form does not change with the person: **jeg jobbet**, **hun jobbet**. In yes/no questions, the verb goes before the subject, with no equivalent of English «did»: **Jobbet du i går?**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Time expressions at the start",
     "texto": [
      "If a time expression comes first, the conjugated verb takes second place: **I går jobbet jeg hjemme**. In English we say «yesterday I worked», with the subject straight after the time expression; in Norwegian the verb comes right after it, so the subject moves after the verb."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
